  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Japchae takes about 45 minutes and serves 4. These "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "glass noodles",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "glass-noodles"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " are made from sweet potato starch. They are chewy and translucent. They soak up the soy and sesame dressing really well."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The most common mistake with japchae is overcooking the noodles before the stir-fry. Soak them until just pliable, not fully soft. They will finish cooking in the wok. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing with sesame oil",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "sesame-oil-finish"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is important: add it off the heat at the end, not at the beginning of cooking."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
